Fix avatarSVG to validate av.bg array and required fields. Use:
```
const base = makeAvatar();
const av = (a && Array.isArray(a.bg)) ? { ...base, ...a, bg: a.bg } : { ...base, ...(a||{}), bg: base.bg };
```
But if a.avatar is an array? In this game avatar is object. If a itself is avatar. `avatarSVG(a)` expects avatar object, not artist. It uses a.bg, a.hair. So ensure bg is array with 2 colors.

Simplest:
```
const av = a && Array.isArray(a.bg) && a.bg.length >= 2 ? a : makeAvatar();
```
But if a has valid bg but missing hair/skin, could still break? hair used in template, skin used. Use fallback defaults:
```
const base = makeAvatar();
const av = { ...base, ...(a && typeof a === 'object' ? a : {}) };
if (!Array.isArray(av.bg) || av.bg.length < 2) av.bg = base.bg;
```
Also accessory/hair could be undefined; set defaults:
```
av.hair ||= base.hair; av.skin ||= base.skin; av.accessory ??= base.accessory; av.style ??= base.style;
```
This makes it robust.

Patch.

input.newString:
export function avatarSVG(a, size = 64, opts = {}) {
  const base = makeAvatar();
  const av = { ...base, ...(a && typeof a === 'object' ? a : {}) };
  if (!Array.isArray(av.bg) || av.bg.length < 2) av.bg = base.bg;
  if (!av.hair) av.hair = base.hair;
  if (!av.skin) av.skin = base.skin;
  if (!Number.isFinite(av.style)) av.style = base.style;
  if (!Number.isFinite(av.accessory)) av.accessory = base.accessory;
  const [c1, c2] = av.bg;

